-- Q2400: Circular 230 [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under Circular 230 Section 10.50(c), censure is the least severe of the three primary disciplinary sanctions and constitutes a public reprimand. Importantly, censure does not restrict or terminate the practitioner''s right to practice before the IRS, unlike suspension or disbarment.
Wrong (B): A temporary prohibition from practicing describes suspension under Section 10.50(a), not censure.
Wrong (C): Circular 230 does not impose monetary penalties equal to the client''s tax deficiency as a disciplinary sanction.
Wrong (D): A permanent prohibition from practicing describes disbarment under Section 10.50(a), the most severe sanction.$EXPL$
