-- Q2401: Circular 230 [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Circular 230 Section 10.23, a practitioner with a valid power of attorney must exercise due diligence by promptly informing the client of IRS correspondence and taking appropriate action within the scope of the engagement. This duty ensures the client''s interests and deadlines are protected.
Wrong (A): Responding without informing the client violates the practitioner''s obligation to keep the client informed of matters affecting their account.
Wrong (B): A practitioner cannot simply ignore IRS notices; the duty of prompt disposition applies regardless of the tax year involved.
Wrong (D): Returning the notice and redirecting correspondence abandons the practitioner''s responsibility under the power of attorney.$EXPL$
