-- Q2402: Circular 230 [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Circular 230 Section 10.29, a practitioner may represent conflicting interests before the IRS if each party provides informed written consent after full disclosure of the conflict. The practitioner must also reasonably believe they can provide competent and diligent representation to each client.
Wrong (A): Dual representation is not automatically prohibited. Section 10.29 permits it with proper disclosure and written consent from each party.
Wrong (B): Spouses are not treated as one taxpayer for conflict-of-interest purposes; each spouse is a separate client requiring individual consent.
Wrong (C): Referral to separate practitioners is not mandatory. The practitioner may continue if informed written consent is obtained from both spouses.$EXPL$
