-- Q2418: Professional Ethics in Tax [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Circular 230 Section 10.21 and AICPA SSTS No. 6, when a CPA discovers that a client used fraudulent information on a return, the CPA must withdraw from the engagement and advise the client to take corrective action. The CPA must not sign any future returns affected by the fraud.
Wrong (A): The CPA cannot continue the engagement simply because the fraud was unknown at filing. Once discovered, the CPA must withdraw and cannot be complicit in ongoing noncompliance.
Wrong (B): Circular 230 does not require the practitioner to report the client directly to law enforcement absent a court order.
Wrong (D): The CPA cannot unilaterally file an amended return without the client''s authorization. The corrective action decision rests with the client.$EXPL$
