-- Q2423: Professional Ethics in Tax [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SSTS No. 1 and IRC Section 280A(c), a home office deduction requires exclusive and regular use for business. When the taxpayer has an employer-provided office, the home office must also meet the convenience-of-the-employer test under Section 280A(c)(1). The CPA must evaluate these requirements before recommending the position.
Wrong (B): Working from home most of the week does not automatically qualify the deduction. The statutory requirements of exclusive use and employer convenience must still be met.
Wrong (C): A blanket refusal is inappropriate. SSTS No. 1 requires the CPA to evaluate whether the position has a reasonable basis before accepting or rejecting it.
Wrong (D): A partial deduction based on days worked at home is not how Section 280A operates. The deduction depends on meeting the statutory tests, not a day-ratio calculation.$EXPL$
