-- Q2425: Professional Ethics in Tax [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under Circular 230 Section 10.34(a), by signing a return as paid preparer, the CPA represents that the return is based on all information known to the practitioner and that the positions taken meet applicable standards, including at minimum a reasonable basis for each position.
Wrong (A): Signing a return does not guarantee freedom from audit. The CPA''s representation relates to the quality and basis of the positions taken, not audit likelihood.
Wrong (B): The CPA is not certifying personal verification of every transaction. The representation is that positions meet applicable standards based on known information.
Wrong (D): Signing the return does not create personal liability for the client''s tax deficiency. The CPA''s liability is limited to preparer penalties for noncompliance with standards.$EXPL$
