-- Q2426: Professional Ethics in Tax [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AICPA SSTS No. 7, when a CPA becomes aware of significant new developments that affect previously provided written advice and maintains an ongoing client relationship, the CPA should consider informing the client of the changed circumstances. This reflects a continuing obligation tied to the advisory relationship.
Wrong (B): While SSTS No. 7 does not impose an absolute mandatory update duty, a CPA with an ongoing relationship should consider updating the client when significant adverse developments arise.
Wrong (C): An amended return is not automatically required. The CPA''s obligation is to inform the client of the changed authority, not to unilaterally file amended returns.
Wrong (D): Waiting for an IRS challenge is not consistent with the CPA''s advisory duty. Proactive communication about adverse developments protects the client''s interests.$EXPL$
