-- Q2427: Professional Ethics in Tax [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AICPA SSTS No. 3, a CPA may generally rely on client-provided information but must not ignore implications of information known to the CPA. When income appears significantly understated, the CPA must make reasonable inquiries, evaluate the reliability of records, and document conclusions.
Wrong (A): Simply accepting records that appear incomplete ignores the CPA''s duty under SSTS No. 3 to inquire when known information raises concerns about reliability.
Wrong (B): The CPA is not required to report the client to the IRS. SSTS No. 3 calls for inquiry and professional judgment, not refusal and reporting.
Wrong (D): Adjusting income to match industry averages has no basis in SSTS No. 3. The CPA should investigate the actual facts rather than apply arbitrary benchmarks.$EXPL$
