-- Q2430: Tax Procedures [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 6501(c), there is no statute of limitations on assessment when the taxpayer files a false or fraudulent return with the intent to evade tax, or when no return is filed at all. The IRS may assess additional tax at any time in these circumstances.
Wrong (B): Filing a late return does not eliminate the statute of limitations. The three-year period generally runs from the actual filing date under Section 6501(a).
Wrong (C): Underpaying estimated taxes does not affect the assessment statute of limitations. Estimated tax penalties are governed separately under Section 6654.
Wrong (D): Claiming too many exemptions does not create an unlimited assessment period. This may trigger other penalties but does not override the standard limitations period.$EXPL$
