  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 6663, the civil fraud penalty is 75% of the underpayment attributable to fraud. The IRS must prove fraud by clear and convincing evidence. This penalty is significantly more severe than the 20% accuracy-related penalty.
Wrong (A): The 20% rate is the accuracy-related penalty under Section 6662 for negligence or substantial understatement, not fraud.
Wrong (C): There is no 50% civil fraud penalty rate in the Internal Revenue Code. Section 6663 specifies 75%.
Wrong (D): The Code does not impose a 100% fraud penalty. The maximum civil fraud penalty rate is 75% of the underpayment attributable to fraud.$EXPL$
