UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRS administrative procedures, a 30-day letter gives the taxpayer 30 days to agree or file a written protest requesting a conference with the IRS Appeals Office under IRC Section 7803(e). This is an administrative appeal that can resolve disputes without litigation.
Wrong (A): The taxpayer is not limited to accepting the proposed changes. The 30-day letter specifically provides the opportunity to request an administrative appeal.
Wrong (B): A Tax Court petition requires a statutory notice of deficiency (90-day letter) under IRC Section 6213(a), not a 30-day letter.
